# routine — learn a Buy routine, then walk it straight into the trade menu
#
# The round trip of the routine system: a routine is learned by playing, the player leaves and comes
# back, and the routine enters its own area and hour in the phase it names — here the trade menu,
# with no walk and no conversation in front of it.
#
# WHAT IS LEARNED. Walking into the wood is not recorded at all. Opening a conversation with the
# farmer teaches a Meet routine; her agreeing to sell teaches a Buy routine (the auto-dialogue path
# reads the same flags the played one does — LocationTravelGameController.RecordAgreementRoutines);
# and leaving from the wood, which is not where the visit opened, teaches a Go to routine.
#
# WHAT ENTERING MUST GET RIGHT. The trade menu is opened from a rebuilt scene, and the rebuild starts
# at the location's default opening area (Test Yard). The routine carries its area so the scene is
# repositioned before the menu opens; `expect-state where Test Wood` at the end is that — without it
# the player would close the menu and find themselves in the yard.
#
# THE SETUP. The farmer sells crops and roams: at noon she is in Test Wood, one plain path from Test
# Yard. --npc-affinity is what makes propose_to_buy possible at all (TradeGate wants an
# acquaintance), and is also what lets the Buy routine be walked. --observe-only pins the FIRST
# phase, in the yard, on the wood; the `observe` command pins the second, in the wood, on the farmer.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --npc-affinity CloseFriend --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon --observe-only "Test Wood"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
strategy succeed

# --- walk into the wood ------------------------------------------------------
goal move
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# Pinned BEFORE the footer press: that press closes the segment and generates the next phase's
# observation, so a filter set after it would arrive too late to steer anything.
# The second phase is clicked into: settle the word-vector load first, or which keyword it
# highlights depends on a race (see `wait embeddings`).
wait embeddings 60
observe farmer
goal propose_to_buy
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
expect-state where Test Wood
# Open ground: the wood is nobody's, so what is learned here can be walked.
expect-state where trespass=no

# --- the trade, which teaches the Meet and the Buy routines -------------------
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# Learned as it happens — asserted by kind and place, never by name: the name carries the
# farmer's rolled name, which is content.
inspect routines
expect-state routines category=meet location=
expect-state routines category=buy location=
expect-state routines Test Wood
expect-state routines time=Noon

# --- leave, go elsewhere, and come back on the routine ------------------------
observe none
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

# Leaving from the wood, not the yard it opened in, is the Go to routine.
expect-state routines category=goto location=

# Routines go into the save as a list of an abstract type, which System.Text.Json drops the fields
# of — and refuses to read back — unless every kind is registered. One unregistered kind would make
# the whole save unloadable; this is the assertion that says so, for the three kinds learned here.
save roundtrip

# The routines menu shows a Buy routine with the merchant's catalogue and their standing with you,
# read from the location's memory without building the scene.
manage Routines buy
wait 10
expect B U Y
expect WHAT THEY SELL
# The line is asserted, not its level: TestSceneFactory spawns its people without the location's
# affinity store (every real factory passes it), so the test location remembers no standing at all.
expect relation:
manage
wait mode WorldView 30

travel neighbour
travel-go
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

travel back
routines
routines buy
wait mode Trading 150

# The point of the whole script: the menu opened in the routine's own area, not the one the rebuilt
# scene opens at.
expect-state where Test Wood
expect-state where period=Noon
quit
